<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 4.648 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 4.648 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 4.648 billion pesos from the secondary market on Tuesday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and seven repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    359 days</p>
<p>    150 million    176 days</p>
<p>    150 million     86 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    600 million     79 days</p>
<p>    600 million     69 days</p>
<p>    700 million     51 days</p>
<p>    700 million     44 days</p>
<p>    700 million     30 days</p>
<p>    700 million     16 days</p>
<p>    198 million	1 day</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( -- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
